ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20356, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01FP6jYTRqNaN6WQXhXsv1yf", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20356, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0117ThpBSjb2G7LTtJS7KRxr", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20656, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0117ThpBSjb2G7LTtJS7KRxr", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20656, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0117ThpBSjb2G7LTtJS7KRxr", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25083, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012diGwu359bumzUVK8Rd5cz", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in production (error rate 18%) in us-east, us-west and eu-west. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback. All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy, with an error rate of 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before it shipped) and investigate the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55683, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012diGwu359bumzUVK8Rd5cz", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55683, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012diGwu359bumzUVK8Rd5cz", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57551, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01UNgRLWQUGkDWUiq9Pcni9s", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57851, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01UNgRLWQUGkDWUiq9Pcni9s", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57851, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01UNgRLWQUGkDWUiq9Pcni9s", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62969, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's now passing health checks. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which pages the on-call engineer.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of 18%.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so it's the version I rolled back to. It had already run healthily there, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, leaving the other two regions on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once and it finished in all regions.\n- All regions are now on v2.3.0, healthy, with an error rate of 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open INC-0001 timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate and no second page.\n- It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial first attempt) and two follow-ups:\n  - Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was already unhealthy in staging before it shipped.\n  - Investigate the deployment-system error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014B7t2aoUX7nPBuCqVxtMFY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UL131GrvwAbzUxpQMieyan", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_014aC7T3PrVoZG4xQwPRnLZY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01BRnqQgbr75cCftr91YQ5qb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012eYkNwNUaQKtWMDjp5dEQq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FP6jYTRqNaN6WQXhXsv1yf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0117ThpBSjb2G7LTtJS7KRxr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012diGwu359bumzUVK8Rd5cz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in production (error rate 18%) in us-east, us-west and eu-west. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on different versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback. All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy, with an error rate of 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging before it shipped) and investigate the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01UNgRLWQUGkDWUiq9Pcni9s", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's now passing health checks. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which pages the on-call engineer.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of 18%.\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so it's the version I rolled back to. It had already run healthily there, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, leaving the other two regions on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once and it finished in all regions.\n- All regions are now on v2.3.0, healthy, with an error rate of 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to open INC-0001 timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate and no second page.\n- It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial first attempt) and two follow-ups:\n  - Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was already unhealthy in staging before it shipped.\n  - Investigate the deployment-system error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}